---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base title="About" description={`About ${site.title}. Replace this page before you publish.`}>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <aside class="edit-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Edit this page before you publish.</strong> It is a placeholder, not a description of a real teacher.
      The file is <code>src/pages/about.astro</code>.
    </p>
  </aside>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Put your name here. Say what you teach, and where people already watch you. You can also add your YouTube,
      Facebook, and GitHub links in <code>site.config.json</code> so they show in the header and footer.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site is a public archive of prompts and numbered steps. Viewers can search it. They do not create an
      account, and there is no dashboard in this template.
    </p>
    <p>The author name in the template is “{site.author}”. Change that before you rely on it.</p>
    <p>Delete these paragraphs and write in your own voice.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
